{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01H1ML6qw4oyWQqdFH62V36b", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://jurnal.uin-antasari.ac.id/index.php/khazanah/article/view/2339\"}, {\"url\": \"https://repository.unsri.ac.id/15312/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://garuda.kemdikbud.go.id/documents/detail/1813856\"}, {\"url\": \"https://jom.unri.ac.id/index.php/JOMFKIP/article/download/12378/12023\"}, {\"url\": \"https://proceedings.radenfatah.ac.id/index.php/isah/article/view/504\"}, {\"url\": \"https://ojs.unimal.ac.id/index.php/jumasi/article/download/10952/6070\"}, {\"url\": \"https://jurnal.ar-raniry.ac.id/index.php/cobaBK/article/download/6766/4647\"}, {\"url\": \"https://journal.unj.ac.id/unj/index.php/isllae/article/download/10867/7372/26029\"}, {\"url\": \"https://ejournal3.undip.ac.id/index.php/sulukindo/article/view/113\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:09:31.691Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Bimbang Bebalai upacara suku", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01USm5qEN3fgzkpJUWph6EwF", "content": [{"title": "MAKNA UPACARA BATIMBANG DALAM TRADISI MASYARAKAT SUKU BANJAR KUALA TUNGKAL, PROVINSI JAMBI", "url": "https://jurnal.uin-antasari.ac.id/index.php/khazanah/article/view/2339"}, {"title": "repository.unsri.ac.id", "url": "https://repository.unsri.ac.id/15312/"}, {"title": "Jurnal Online Mahasiswa (JOM) Bidang Keguruan dan Ilmu Pendidikan", "url": "https://garuda.kemdikbud.go.id/documents/detail/1813856"}, {"title": "jom.unri.ac.id", "url": "https://jom.unri.ac.id/index.php/JOMFKIP/article/download/12378/12023"}, {"title": "ISLAMIC VALUE IN MELAYU’S BIMBANG TRADITION", "url": "https://proceedings.radenfatah.ac.id/index.php/isah/article/view/504"}, {"title": "unimal.ac.id", "url": "https://ojs.unimal.ac.id/index.php/jumasi/article/download/10952/6070"}, {"title": "ar-raniry.ac.id", "url": "https://jurnal.ar-raniry.ac.id/index.php/cobaBK/article/download/6766/4647"}, {"title": "journal.unj.ac.id", "url": "https://journal.unj.ac.id/unj/index.php/isllae/article/download/10867/7372/26029"}, {"title": "BibTex Citation Data :", "url": "https://ejournal3.undip.ac.id/index.php/sulukindo/article/view/113"}]}, "The search turned up no article specifically about a \"Bimbang Balai\" ceremony for a suku, but several related results came up.\n\n- **Bimbang Balai in Jeranglah Village (South Bengkulu):** A study of this custom examines how the ceremony is carried out and what has caused it to shift. It uses historical, anthropological, and social approaches, with questionnaires and interviews of residents aged 40 and over. The research is titled \"Indigenous Shifi in Balancing hall in Jeranglah Village, Manna District, South Bengkulu Regency in 1990-2017.\" The problems raised in this study are how the implementation process of Bimbang Balai Custom works and what causes a shift in the Bimbang Balai Custom.\n- **Bimbang in Bengkulu Malay tradition:** This is a ceremony that is held to celebrate various moments such as inauguration, marriage, and the appointment of traditional heads. This culture shows the cycle of life.\n- **Batimbang in Banjar Kuala Tungkal (Jambi):** This is a different rite, aimed at children born in the Safar month. It is only intended for babies who are born in the Safar month of the Hijri calendar. It is meant to ward off misfortune.\n\nThe results don't say which suku the Bimbang Balai ceremony belongs to, so a follow-up search on the Jeranglah or South Bengkulu customary community, or on the full text of the Jeranglah study, would be needed to confirm that."], "durationSeconds": 7.695650541000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01H1ML6qw4oyWQqdFH62V36b", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
