{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01M5nEbaa9krdJKS5M7vrHv4", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://budaya-indonesia.org/bimbang-bebalai\"}, {\"url\": \"https://handep.kemdikbud.go.id/index.php/handep/article/view/131\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/391031854_PUDARNYA_TRADISI_BIMBANG_ADAT_DALAM_UPACARA_PERNIKAHAN\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.academia.edu/44859397/TRADISI_BIMBANG_BEBALAI_PADA_ETNIS_SERAWAI_SEBUAH_ANALISIS_FUNGSIONAL_STRUKTURAL_BIMBANG_BEBALAI_TRADITION_AMONG_THE_SERAWAI_A_STRUCTURAL_FUNCTIONAL_ANALYSIS\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.academia.edu/69599663/Makna_Tari_Napa_Pada_Bimbang_Adat_Suku_Serawai_DI_Kota_Manna_Kabupaten_Bengkulu_Selatan\"}, {\"url\": \"http://repository.iainbengkulu.ac.id/8181/1/REKA%20OKTAVIA.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://budaya-indonesia.org/Adat-Pernikahan-Suku-Serawai-Kabupaten-Seluma-Bengkulu\"}, {\"url\": \"https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bimbang_Bebalai\"}, {\"url\": \"http://pustaka-bpkxii.org/pustaka/adat-istiadat-perkawinan-suku-serawai-bengkulu-selatan\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:09:52.121Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "bimbang bebalai adat perkawinan suku Serawai Bengkulu Selatan", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01VXa7uK75HFizRWQXtEtkwK", "content": [{"title": "Bimbang Bebalai » Budaya Indonesia", "url": "https://budaya-indonesia.org/bimbang-bebalai"}, {"title": "TRADISI BIMBANG BEBALAI PADA ETNIS SERAWAI: SEBUAH ANALISIS FUNGSIONAL STRUKTURAL", "url": "https://handep.kemdikbud.go.id/index.php/handep/article/view/131"}, {"title": "(PDF) PUDARNYA TRADISI BIMBANG ADAT DALAM UPACARA PERNIKAHAN", "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/391031854_PUDARNYA_TRADISI_BIMBANG_ADAT_DALAM_UPACARA_PERNIKAHAN"}, {"title": "(PDF) TRADISI BIMBANG BEBALAI PADA ETNIS SERAWAI: SEBUAH ANALISIS FUNGSIONAL STRUKTURAL BIMBANG BEBALAI TRADITION AMONG THE SERAWAI: A STRUCTURAL FUNCTIONAL ANALYSIS", "url": "https://www.academia.edu/44859397/TRADISI_BIMBANG_BEBALAI_PADA_ETNIS_SERAWAI_SEBUAH_ANALISIS_FUNGSIONAL_STRUKTURAL_BIMBANG_BEBALAI_TRADITION_AMONG_THE_SERAWAI_A_STRUCTURAL_FUNCTIONAL_ANALYSIS"}, {"title": "(PDF) Makna Tari Napa Pada Bimbang Adat Suku Serawai DI Kota Manna Kabupaten Bengkulu Selatan", "url": "https://www.academia.edu/69599663/Makna_Tari_Napa_Pada_Bimbang_Adat_Suku_Serawai_DI_Kota_Manna_Kabupaten_Bengkulu_Selatan"}, {"title": "DINAMIKA TRADISI PERNIKAHAN SUKU SERAWAI DI", "url": "http://repository.iainbengkulu.ac.id/8181/1/REKA%20OKTAVIA.pdf"}, {"title": "Adat Pernikahan Suku Serawai Kabupaten Seluma Bengkulu » Budaya Indonesia", "url": "https://budaya-indonesia.org/Adat-Pernikahan-Suku-Serawai-Kabupaten-Seluma-Bengkulu"}, {"title": "Bimbang Bebalai - Wikipedia bahasa Indonesia, ensiklopedia bebas", "url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bimbang_Bebalai"}, {"title": "ADAT ISTIADAT PERKAWINAN SUKU SERAWAI BENGKULU SELATAN", "url": "http://pustaka-bpkxii.org/pustaka/adat-istiadat-perkawinan-suku-serawai-bengkulu-selatan"}]}, "Search results on the Serawai *bimbang bebalai* wedding tradition are mostly Indonesian-language sources, and they agree on the core features:\n\n- **What it is:** Bimbang Bebalai is a wedding ceremony held in a hall or special place built by the community through mutual help. The akad nikah (marriage contract) is held at the bride's home.\n- **Scale and food:** Several couples, typically 3 to 5, are married together around the same time. A buffalo must be slaughtered, with the thigh shared among the helpers and the rest cooked to feed guests.\n- **Participants:** Customary institutions, the traditional ruler (rajo pengulu), government representatives, and community leaders are expected to attend.\n- **Decline:** A 2020 study in Handep journal found the tradition cannot currently be carried out because the indigenous institutions and structures that support it no longer function. Another study on Semidang Alas, Seluma, reports that the bimbang adat stage has disappeared since around 2000, and it links this to modernization and younger people losing interest.\n- **Documentation:** A 1985 book by Mustakim Usman describes the full sequence, from courtship visits at night to the wedding day, and notes that every stage must follow the prescribed customs.\n\nCaveat: the sources differ on location. Some place the tradition in Seluma Regency, which was split from South Bengkulu, while others cover the wider Serawai area of Bengkulu Selatan. The best overall source is the 2020 Handep article (handep.kemdikbud.go.id), which is an academic study."], "durationSeconds": 10.662869041000002, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01M5nEbaa9krdJKS5M7vrHv4", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
